  ImageLeft: {fileID: 0}
  Title: 'Mode Of Transmission:'
  Description: (Bullet and Fluid beam) Person-to-person transmission occurs via close
    personal contact with an infected individual or their body fluids. Principle routes
    of infection include inoculation, mucous membranes, and abraded or injured skin.
    Nosocomial infections can occur through direct contact with infected body fluids,
    for example due to the reuse of unsterilized syringes, needles, or other medical
    equipment contaminated with these fluids.
